editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The pin-after-push red, and the spine guard that refused a hundred and third row
prompt Close the round; standfast on reds found in the round itself.
think Reading `.claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md` after fold L's push rather than before it showed the order had been broken: stage, commit, amend once so the nib names HEAD, never a pin-only follow-up. Fold L ran commit, then push, then noticed the card still named `c352a3b7ee` -- the commit before the round it describes.
think The only sanctioned repair after a push is a force-push, which `.claude/rules/send-word.md` reserves for Keaton's explicit word. So the repair had to be the one the rules actually allow: correct the nib in the working tree and let it ride the next work commit, which is exactly the lag the pin rule tolerates when it says not to chase a fixed-point hash.
think Booked it as REDS %103 rather than fixing it quietly. REDS %84's whole lesson is that the ledger is part of the fix, since the next reader inherits the ledger rather than the commit that repaired something in silence.
obs Adding the row made `reds_ledger_monotone_witness` refuse by name -- it pins the row count it reached, so a spine that grows past the pin is a red rather than a quieter GREEN. That is precisely what REDS %102 rebuilt it to do two laps ago, and this is the first time the rebuilt behavior fired on a real row. A guard earning its keep on the lap after it was hardened is the cheapest possible proof that the hardening was real.
obs The red is a process slip rather than a defect in the tree, and it is worth the row anyway. An ordered rule is only kept if the order is read before the first step; the amend is a step inside a send, not a tidy-up after one.
loom reds rows=103 ledger_bytes=21690 bound=24576
file crux/REDS.md row %103 -- what went wrong, what caught it, what it taught
file crux/REMEMBER.md the nib corrected to `253a714cce`, riding a work commit rather than a pin-only one
file tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish repinned from measurement, GREEN at 1..103
recommend keep-going the fold queue the new meter prints stands ready and mechanical -- `mend_the_plan` at 36 rungs by 178 lines, 6,230 carried. Read the pin rule's order before the first step of the next send, not after the last.
